Welcome to the "To-Do List" Application.

Application usage is as follows: 
After intializing the app users will be shown a menu. Inputing the number of the menu item will open the associated function.
(1) Will ask users if they would like to add a task to their list. A simple yes or no is all that is required. If yes is input, then the function will ask what the task to be added to the list is. If no is input, the task adding function will end and return the user to the main menu.
(2) Will print the current list itemized and then return the user to the main menu. 
(3) Will display the current to-do list and then ask the user to select which task has been completed by inputing the listed number associated with the task. When the user inputs a task line number that exists in the "To-Do" list, the task will be removed from that list, and added to a new list titled "Completed Tasks". The "To-Do" and  "Completed" will then be printed and the user will be returned to the main menu. 
(4) Will display the current "To-Do" list and ask the user which task they would like to delete a task. The user selects the appropriate number for the task they would like to delete. As long as that task exists in the list, the task will be deleted, a current task list will be printed, and the user will be returned to the main menu.
(5) Will exit the app. 
